Hi,

I've got a new patch that swaps the y and z keys for the key layouts
that need it. It's different from GERMANKB in that it uses a run-time
option (you will need to set QWERTZ at compile-time to enable this
option).

This is useful mainly if somebody wants to build a binary which is
going to be used by different people and/or run on different machines
(via NFS for example).

http://home.in.tum.de/~traykovs/nethack/qwertz-343.diff

It did itch to build in dynamic key-binding support, but for this some
decisions mildly but globally affecting the whole game need to be
taken which are not for me to take. Does anybody know if this is
planned by the DevTeam?

PS: Jukka: I think I made the diff to patch cleanly atop of your
combined diff, if GERMANKB weren't present, should you choose to
replace it.

